+- Add {attr}`Parameter.spec`, how the user spells the parameter on the command line:
+  `--times` for `-t, --times`, `FILENAME` for an argument. Deprecation messages
+  name an option by its spec, so a deprecated `--my-option` shows as
+  `'--my-option'` rather than `'my_option'`, and so does the "is deprecated and
+  still required" error. An option declared only with a secondary spelling, such
+  as `click.option("name", " /--no-name", required=True)`, now reports
+  `Missing option '--no-name'.` rather than `'name'`.
+- {meth}`Parameter.get_help_spec` moved from {class}`Option` to {class}`Parameter`,
+  which returns {attr}`spec`. {class}`Argument` overrides it to return its metavar.
+- {attr}`Parameter.human_readable_name` is deprecated in favor of {attr}`spec`. It
+  still returns `spec`. A subclass that overrides it gets a `DeprecationWarning`
+  when the class is defined, so override `spec` instead.
 
